      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-341495",
      ":question/problem": "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ if $f(x)=4\\sqrt{x}+3tan⁡x.$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We know that $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(tan⁡x)={sec}^{2}⁡x.$ Applying these formulas, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4\\sqrt{x}+3tan⁡x) \\\\  & =4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x})+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(tan⁡x) \\\\  & =4(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}})+3({sec}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}}+3{sec}^{2}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
