      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-47983",
      ":question/problem": "Find the derivative of $y=\\sqrt{x}+tan⁡x.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We know that $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(tan⁡x)={sec}^{2}⁡x.$ Applying this formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x}+tan⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}+{sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{1+2\\sqrt{x}{sec}^{2}⁡x}{2\\sqrt{x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
